    "title": "Whitley County Plan Commission hosts listening session for potential data center - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Gracie Sherrow ,\n2 hours ago\nWHITLEY COUNTY, Ind. (WANE) – The Whitley County Plan Commission hosted a gathering on Wednesday to gather community input for the potential of a new zoning code tailored to data center developments.\nThe public listening session was held at 7 p.m. on Wednesday after the Plan Commission meeting at the Whitley County Government Center; no votes or decisions were made.\nOfficials say the meeting was a preemptive exploration of dedicated zoning standards and regulations as data center developments increase in Indiana. Feedback from the community will be used to help guide discussions on how data centers might fit into the county’s future growth.\nPublic comment will continue to be accepted through July 6.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
    "summary": "(WANE) – The Whitley County Plan Commission hosted a gathering on Wednesday to gather community input for the potential of a new zoning code tailored to data center developments. The public listening session was held at 7 p.m. on Wednesday after the Plan Commission meeting at the Whitley County Government Center; no votes or decisions were made. Officials say the meeting was a preemptive exploration of dedicated zoning standards and regulations as data center developments increase in Indiana. Feedback from the community will be used to help guide discussions on how data centers might fit into the county’s future growth.",
